error[ffi_lock_copied]: `made` returns a `Box`, whose C struct `struct box` holds a `pthread_mutex_t` at `m`, a copy out of its place, which C forbids
  at tests/golden/unsupported/ffi-lock-copied-a-result.hero:12:10
     |
  12 | function made() -> Box  #~ ffi_lock_copied
     |          ^^^^
  note: a copy of a lock is a second lock holding the first one's state: the copy of a held mutex reads held, and unlocking one leaves the other locked
  note: build it where it lives, `c: T @= T(...)`, then hand it to a function that takes `@c`
  note: lend the place instead: a function taking `@c` receives the caller's own cell, `f(@c)`; a field is read in place, `c.n`

